# Private scanner patterns. Copy to scripts/patterns.private and fill in.
#
#   cp scripts/patterns.private.example scripts/patterns.private
#
# patterns.private is gitignored and must stay that way. It holds the literal strings
# that must never be published, which is exactly why it cannot be a tracked file: a
# tracked pattern list puts every secret it protects into the permanent history of the
# repo it is protecting.
#
# Format matches the PATTERNS array in scan-secrets.sh: one "label|regex" per line.
# The regex is PCRE, passed to grep -P. Escape backslashes once, not twice — this file
# is read as plain text, not as bash source.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.

# Business name (must never appear)|(?i)\b<BUSINESS_NAME>\b
# Internal bot name (say 'Telegram alerts')|(?i)<BOT_NAME>
# Personal phone number|\b<AREA>[.\ -]?<PREFIX>[.\ -]?<LINE>\b
# Employer name|(?i)\b<EMPLOYER>\b
# Real first and last name of anyone but the author|(?i)\b<FIRST> <LAST>\b
